WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.960
New York just banned ai chatbot toys for kids for the next five years. This is Models &amp; Agents for Beginners, Episode 239. Still ahead, a deep dive on an ai that checks its own code. Cool stuff and try this with a ChatGPT adventure mode, and quick bits. Governor Kathy Hoke will sign the measure, in-gadget reports, covering physical toys that talk back to children through a chatbot. A chatbot is software that holds a conversation, and these toys use artificial intelligence or ai to invent replies instead of

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:35.080
playing a recorded line. Sales are on hold while researchers study how a talking toy changes

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.420
the way kids grow, chat, and feel. Picture a brand new playground ride that answers when

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:45.700
you speak, with a stop sign in front until grown-ups know it belongs there. Common sense media

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:50.100
found safety failures, including kids seeing content that does not belong in a child's

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:55.080
room, and risks to how they learn to handle feelings. The same research warns the toys

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:57.780
can change how kids practice talking with actual people.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:02.640
Talking toys advertised around the holidays will not sit on New York shells for a while.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:07.100
Companies that build products for children are being told that safety rules are on the way.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:11.260
Families can use the moment to talk about what AI tools are doing in a chat.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:16.560
The wait lets researchers gather real data on how these toys shape conversations and feelings.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:21.280
If you are curious how a rule like this is written, read the full law on the New York

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.460
State government website.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.280
The rule covers sales inside the state and shops that ship to New York addresses have

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:32.220
to follow it too. Toy makers will need to redesign or wait before they can sell again in that

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:38.301
market. Claude wrote a first pass of a live customer doorway in about a week, and Thropic shares,

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:43.621
then needed proof the new code match the old. That doorway is called the Messages API,

00:01:44.241 --> 00:01:49.201
which is the main path customers use to reach Claude, along with Anthropics own apps such as

00:01:49.201 --> 00:01:55.101
Claude code and co-work. Checking a finished Sudoku grid is the easy part, because you only count

00:01:55.101 --> 00:02:00.381
whether each row, column and box has the right numbers. Finding the solution in the first place

00:02:00.381 --> 00:02:05.541
can take a long time. A lot of hard problems work that way, and people call it a generator

00:02:05.541 --> 00:02:11.241
verifier gap, meaning it is often simpler to check an answer than to invent one. Claude has

00:02:11.241 --> 00:02:16.161
used that gap on jobs like turning math arguments into strict proofs, and on moving big,

00:02:16.341 --> 00:02:20.181
well-tested piles of code, as long as a checker could say yes or no.

00:02:20.181 --> 00:02:25.321
Live systems flip the difficulty because writing new code can be the easy step

00:02:25.321 --> 00:02:28.501
while deciding what correct even means is the hard one.

00:02:28.941 --> 00:02:34.441
Users lean on odd little quirks that tests never listed, so a checklist cannot cover every case.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:38.781
And Thropic ran into that when it moved the messages path from Python to Rust,

00:02:39.321 --> 00:02:44.921
to programming languages, with Rust chosen because it can spend far less computer effort on each request.

00:02:44.921 --> 00:02:50.961
Traffic through that path grew roughly 1,800 times from early 2024 to fall

00:02:51.621 --> 00:02:56.581
2026. Trust was still hard because the Python version kept changing, so the

00:02:56.581 --> 00:03:00.821
target moved while they worked. Claude can also answer the same question two

00:03:00.821 --> 00:03:05.301
different ways, so a mismatch is not always a bug. The team could not read

00:03:05.301 --> 00:03:09.201
customer messages so they could not hunt for gaps by looking at what people

00:03:09.201 --> 00:03:14.081
typed. They turned the live messages path itself into the checker, ran the new

00:03:14.081 --> 00:03:19.761
Rust version on real traffic, spotted where the two disagreed, and sent extra AI helpers

00:03:19.761 --> 00:03:21.561
called agents to fix those spots.

00:03:22.161 --> 00:03:27.501
The Rust version now uses about 70% less computer effort per request, and the middle of the

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:31.741
pack weight before the first scrap of a reply appears is about 20% shorter.

00:03:32.401 --> 00:03:36.721
Users kept chatting the whole time, and new features did not freeze while the swap happened.

00:03:37.361 --> 00:03:41.901
A builder that invents, plus a checker that only hunts for differences, is a lot of the

00:03:41.901 --> 00:03:43.481
reason that swap could be trusted.

00:03:44.499 --> 00:03:50.279
Chat GPT added, make a day do anything, a post on X lays out, which takes a regular activity

00:03:50.279 --> 00:03:55.019
like walking to school or eating lunch, and suggests small twists that feel like a story.

00:03:55.559 --> 00:04:00.099
You do not need to learn special prompts or settings, and basic use does not require

00:04:00.099 --> 00:04:00.739
an account.

00:04:01.359 --> 00:04:06.039
It expands a short description of a routine into a sequence of tiny, story-like moments

00:04:06.039 --> 00:04:07.799
you could actually do the same day.

00:04:07.799 --> 00:04:13.179
A bus ride can come back as a treasure hunt with a clue at every stop, still grounded in

00:04:13.179 --> 00:04:13.819
real life.

00:04:14.259 --> 00:04:19.579
Open chat GPT on your phone or computer, type the words, make a day do anything, then

00:04:19.579 --> 00:04:24.579
a daily habit such as walking the dog after school, and notice how playful the ideas stay.

00:04:25.239 --> 00:04:28.139
Pick one or two suggestions and try them before the day ends.

00:04:28.559 --> 00:04:32.879
If you like storytelling or journaling, a boring commute becomes a quick creative drill,

00:04:32.879 --> 00:04:37.259
and you can hop back to ordinary questions in the same chat GPT screen.

00:04:38.248 --> 00:04:42.748
Apple pulled the Mini Max AI chat bot from its App Store, Yahoo Finance Notes,

00:04:43.088 --> 00:04:45.068
over worries about chats with younger users.

00:04:45.668 --> 00:04:49.448
The app had been available to download, then came down after safety reviews

00:04:49.448 --> 00:04:51.508
raised concerns about child interactions.

00:04:52.208 --> 00:04:56.748
The move adds to growing attention on keeping AI tools safe when kids might use them.

